    <string name="about_section_privacy">Privacy policy</string>
    <string name="about_section_perms">Permissions</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_text">Last updated: 23 November 2026\n\nPlayTube needs no account and does not collect, sell or share personal data. It has no ads, no analytics and no tracking. The developer receives no data from the app.\n\nStored only on your device\nWatch history, search history, subscriptions, playlists, favorites, watch later, downloads, settings and local crash logs. Crash logs are shared only when you choose to share them. You can erase everything in Settings → Clear data, and uninstalling the app removes it all.\n\nNetwork connections the app makes\n• YouTube and Google servers (youtube.com, googlevideo.com, ytimg.com) to search, load videos, comments, thumbnails and streams. Like any browser, these servers see your IP address.\n• SponsorBlock (sponsor.ajay.app), only when enabled: it receives the first 4 characters of a hash of the video ID, never the full ID or who you are.\n• lrclib.net, for lyrics: it receives the song title, channel name and duration.\n• The update server (hosted on Cloudflare): the app fetches a small version file when it opens, and downloads the new APK when you update. The server can see your IP address.\n• Telegram and GitHub links open in your browser or app only when you tap them.\n\nVoice search uses the speech-recognition service on your phone, which follows its own provider\'s privacy policy.\n\nPlayTube is not directed at children. This policy changes only with a new app release.\n\nContact: Telegram @YellowlFlash</string>
    <string name="about_perms_text">Internet and network state: load content and detect Wi-Fi.\nNotifications and foreground service: playback controls while the app is in the background.\nWake lock: keep playing with the screen off.\nInstall packages: only to install an update that you approve.</string>
